<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later

  LaunchAgent for the macOS broker-host daemon (librescrs-agent). Bundled as a
  resource in the LibreMac host's Contents/Library/LaunchAgents/, where
  SMAppService.agent(plistName:) registers it. No socket-activation, no
  per-user path templating.

  Self-bind: the agent resolves the App-Group container socket at runtime
  ($HOME/Library/Group Containers/group.org.librescrs.LibreMac/agent.sock) and
  bind()s it itself, so there is NO Sockets key. SMAppService cannot carry a
  per-user SockPathName, which is precisely why socket-activation is off the
  modern path; self-bind resolves the conflict. The container does not exist
  until the sandboxed host first runs, so the host creates it (+ primes the CTK
  registration) and THEN registers/loads this agent.

  RunAtLoad + KeepAlive keep the agent up so it holds the CTK identity and
  observes card presence; it idles cheaply (the per-reader CardSessionHolder
  releases PC/SC after ~45 s). KeepAlive restarts it only after an exit that
  was not clean: an agent stopped on purpose (SIGTERM, a clean quiesce, exit
  status 0) stays stopped, where an unconditional KeepAlive would start it
  again at once. A crash or a refused start is restarted, no sooner than
  ThrottleInterval seconds after the last start.

  Two refused starts repeat by design, and are not a crash loop. An agent
  built with a team id but not signed by that team exits 2 at its start-up
  self-check; one that finds another agent already serving the socket (a
  development run started by hand) exits 3. launchd starts either one again
  every ThrottleInterval seconds, for as long as the cause lasts, and each
  start logs that cause again. The first stops only when the agent is signed
  correctly; the second ends by itself, since the next start after the other
  instance exits takes over the socket.

  ProgramArguments points at the librescrs-agent inside the host bundle
  (Contents/MacOS). The dev harness (packaging/install-dev.sh) substitutes the
  installed libexec path for a standalone launchd smoke.

  No EnvironmentVariables: the agent reads no configuration from its
  environment, since `launchctl setenv` reaches every job the user's launchd
  starts. The bundled agent finds its plugins next to itself; a development
  build is told where they are with the plugin-dir argument, which the dev
  harness adds to ProgramArguments together with the one variable a
  development build needs to start at all (DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH).
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>org.librescrs.agent</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>@LIBRESCRS_AGENT_PROGRAM@</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <dict>
        <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
        <false/>
    </dict>

    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>10</integer>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Interactive</string>
</dict>
</plist>
